{# The canvas home (the contract is BIBLE.md). routes/home.js serves this
   to modern browsers; curl and retro clients keep the plain-text / HTML 3.2
   variants in pages/home.njk. Scripts and styles are real files (CSP:
   script-src 'self'): app.js for behavior, canvas-tokens.css for every
   token, canvas-home.css for the shell, so the guards can scan them. #}
<!doctype html>
{# Two states the SERVER is the only honest source for.
   canvas-pending: the canvas has not painted. True of every page at the
   moment it is parsed, and app.js clears it once render() has seated the
   world. Stamped here rather than by the script, because a script that
   fails is exactly the case the class exists to cover.
   sheet-open: this route SSRs its entry already open. app.js used to add it
   on boot, which left the watch's one-layer rules unarmed for a direct load
   until a script it does not need decided to run.
   item-open: the open sheet is an entry, the layer above the canvas and its
   collections; the bar is not drawn over it (#300). Stamped here for the
   same reason: a direct load must not flash the bar over the page. #}
<html lang="en" class="canvas-pending{% if sheet %} sheet-open{% endif %}{% if sheet and sheet.full %} fullpage-open{% endif %}{% if sheet and sheet.item %} item-open{% endif %}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
{% include "partials/importmap.njk" %}
{# Pinch-zoom stays allowed (WCAG 1.4.4): the scene owns its gestures via
   touch-action, so zoom never needed banning in the first place. #}
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover">
{# NOTE: no disabled-adaptations tag here, on purpose. It used to opt the
   watch out of watchOS's adapted layout, because the adapted 320px page
   broke position:fixed and the modal rendered beside the canvas. The opt-out
   bought a true device width WIDER than the watch threshold in
   canvas-home.css, so the watch was served the phone build: bar, menu,
   booting canvas, fixed layers, everything piled and overflowing. The
   position:fixed failure it was hired to fix has since been retired by the
   one-layer block, which leaves nothing on that screen positioned or
   transformed at all. So the watch gets the adaptation every other site
   gets, and the page it adapts is an ordinary document. #}
{% include "partials/meta-head.njk" %}
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any">
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">
<link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json">
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/dotgothic16-regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
{# Before the module on purpose: the failure it reports is a throw at app.js
   module scope, which is earlier than anything app.js could install. #}
<script src="{{ asset('/canvas/watchdog.js') }}"></script>
<script defer src="{{ asset('/js/sw-register.js') }}"></script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/primitives/kit/canvas-tokens.css') }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/css/ptitle.css') }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/css/canvas-home.css') }}">
{# the kit's parts at their hashes (#313, #319): a sheet that wears the kit
   (an experiment's controls) reads them as --kp-<part>-<state>, opened from the
   canvas or loaded direct, so kit.css never writes an /img URL #}
{% include "kit/parts.njk" %}
{# the kit (#313): the one set of controls; presence's tag and list wear it (#336) #}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/primitives/kit/kit.css') }}">
{# the reader's settings on a page that is read (Dark Mode, Plain Type,
   Listen), scoped to #modal.reading; in the head rather than the entry's
   chain so a reader whose OS is dark never sees the page white first #}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/css/page-reader.css') }}">
{# With JS off the canvas cannot paint, but the prelude is the document:
   the statement, the zones' words, the index and real links. Drop the
   chrome only JS can drive (the field, the close, the map). Placed AFTER the
   canvas-home.css link on purpose: the prelude reveal shares a selector with
   that stylesheet's display:none, so source order is the whole ballgame. #}
<noscript><style>#close,#searchWrap,#minimap{display:none}#prelude{position:fixed;inset:0;display:block;overflow:auto;padding:var(--cv-air) var(--cv-sp-8)}</style></noscript>
{# The three doors are the three most-clicked links; their SSR payloads are
   cheap. This earns the 'inline-speculation-rules' CSP allowance that was
   sitting unused. #}
<script type="speculationrules">{{ speculationRules | safe }}</script>
{# An SSR'd entry sheet ships its stylesheet chain as real links (data-sheet-css
   lets app.js seed its adopted set) and any runtime payload preloads. #}
{%- if sheetAssets %}
{% for href in sheetAssets.css %}<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ href }}" data-sheet-css>
{% endfor -%}
{% for href in sheetAssets.preload %}<link rel="preload" href="{{ href }}" as="fetch">
{% endfor -%}
{% endif %}
</head>
<body>
  {# The tiles mount into #scene, which precedes the topbar in the DOM, so a
     keyboard user tabbed through two dozen tiles before reaching the doors.
     Target depends on what the page IS: a route that SSRs a sheet has its
     content in #sheet (already tabindex=-1); the bare canvas has none, so
     the useful destination is the nav. Hidden until focused, so it adds no
     chrome to the canvas. #}
  <a class="skip k-btn k-solid" href="{% if sheet %}#sheet{% else %}#search{% endif %}">skip to {% if sheet %}content{% else %}search{% endif %}</a>
  <div id="stage">
  {# Depth is resolution (BIBLE.md section 9): whatever you are not reading is
     drawn one step coarser, the same pixels bigger, never a blur. Two cell
     sizes, both WORLD px because the filter runs in #scene's own space: 24
     behind a fan, 48 (one module a cell) behind a sheet. Each filter samples
     one pixel per cell (the flood is the sample, the composite sizes the
     cell, the tile repeats it, the second composite keeps the source under
     the samples) and dilates it out to the cell's edges. The svg is size
     zero and carries only definitions. #}
  {# role=main, not <main>: app.js reads #scene as a positioned layer and sets
     .inert on it while a sheet is open, so the element's box is load-bearing
     and swapping the tag risks the layout. The role is what assistive tech
     needs - the page had nav and dialog landmarks but no main, so there was
     no way to jump to the canvas itself. #}
  <div id="scene" role="main" aria-label="canvas">
    {# The statement, server-rendered: the home document's real h1. No-JS,
       reader mode, and crawlers get the identity line; app.js paints the
       same phrase into the hero on boot and removes this, so nothing ever
       flashes blank. The phrase must match PHRASES[0] in canvas/hero-cycle.js.

       `index` (routes/home.js, `/` only) carries the same collection the
       canvas paints as tiles. Without it the home document was one h1 and
       three links, so a crawler that does not run JS - which is every LLM
       crawler - had nothing to read on the page it fetches first. Routes
       that SSR a sheet (/work, /feed, /about) already ship their prose and
       pass no index, so this never doubles anything.

       A route that SSRs a sheet has its title as the document's h1 already,
       so here the statement is a line and not a second h1. #}
    <div id="prelude">
      {% set statementTag = 'p' if sheet else 'h1' %}
      <{{ statementTag }}>Everyone here sees your cursor.</{{ statementTag }}>
      {%- if boot and boot.zones %}
      {# the zones (BIBLE.md section 5) stand on the ground for a JS visitor;
         here they stand in the document, so a crawler and a no-JS reader get
         the same words and links #}
      <div id="preludeZones">
        {%- for z in boot.zones %}
        <section class="prelude-zone"><h2>{{ z.label }}</h2>{{ z.html | safe }}</section>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- if index %}
      <div id="preludeIndex">
        <p class="prelude-line">Site of {{ identity.author.name }}. {{ identity.tagline }}</p>
        <nav class="prelude-doors" aria-label="sections"><a href="/work">work</a><a href="/feed">feed</a><a href="/about">about</a></nav>
        {%- if index.caseStudies.length %}
        <h2>Case Studies</h2>
        <ul>
          {%- for e in index.caseStudies %}
          <li><a href="{{ e.href }}">{{ e.title }}</a>{% if e.summary %} <span>{{ e.summary }}</span>{% endif %}</li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if index.entries.length %}
        <h2>Writing &amp; Web</h2>
        <ul>
          {%- for e in index.entries %}
          <li><a href="{{ e.href }}"{% if e.external %} rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ e.title }}</a>{% if e.summary %} <span>{{ e.summary }}</span>{% endif %}</li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        {%- endif %}
        <h2>Reach Me</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="mailto:{{ identity.author.email }}">{{ identity.author.email }}</a></li>
          {%- for name, href in identity.social %}
          <li><a href="{{ href }}" rel="noopener">{{ name }}</a></li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {# The plan (#303): past the mount floor nothing mounts and app.js paints
     the world here instead, on the map's cell, at camera scale. It takes no
     pointer; the scene under it keeps every gesture. #}
  <canvas id="plan" aria-hidden="true" hidden></canvas>
  {# The screen chrome is one landmark: the finder, the map and the close are
     the ways around the canvas, and outside every landmark a reader moving
     by landmarks never met them. A plain box: the bar and the map stay fixed
     layers and siblings (the phone's shared slot is `#topbar ~ #minimap`),
     so wrapping them moves nothing. #}
  <nav>
  <div id="topbar">
    {# The bar is the field (BIBLE.md section 8, 2026-09-10). The home
       button and the menu left it: the doors are the sections, the bulb is
       on the ground, home is Esc, /home or a tap on the map. #}
    {# A phone's middle slot is shared (#303): the field comes in from the
       left, the map from the right, one up at a time. This is the left
       column's way back to the field; a desktop keeps the field up and has
       no use for it. #}
    <button id="findBtn" class="k-btn k-ico" type="button" aria-label="search" aria-controls="searchWrap" hidden><svg viewBox="0 0 11 11" shape-rendering="crispEdges" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M2 0h3v1h-3zM1 1h1v1h-1zM5 1h1v1h-1zM0 2h1v3h-1zM6 2h1v3h-1zM1 5h1v1h-1zM5 5h1v1h-1zM2 6h3v1h-3zM6 6h2v1h-2zM7 7h2v1h-2zM8 8h2v1h-2zM9 9h2v2h-2z"/></svg></button>
    <div id="searchWrap">
      {# the search is a FINDER (2026-09-11): typing takes the camera to the
         top result and lights it; the arrows walk the rest, Enter goes in.
         One line over the field says which of how many. #}
      <div id="found" aria-live="polite" hidden></div>
      {# the kit's field (#336), boxed: one-cell lines on all four sides
         (a rule under the words alone blended into the world under the
         bar), and the block caret after the words, blinking in a step
         while the field has focus #}
      <div class="k-field k-sm k-boxed" id="searchField"><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="search or /" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" aria-label="search or command" role="combobox" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cmds" aria-autocomplete="list"><span class="k-caret"></span></div>
      {# the command roster: the one popup the bar still owns. "/" opens it,
         text past the slash filters it; plain text never opens it (the
         lens owns plain text). The kit's menu, opening upward off the
         bar, its best row nearest the field. #}
      <div id="cmds" class="k-menu k-up" role="listbox" aria-label="commands"></div>
    </div>
    {# the right inset's column: the map's toggle at rest, and a close in
       its place while a sheet or a fan is up (app.js syncClose) #}
    <button id="mapBtn" class="k-btn k-ico" type="button" aria-label="map" aria-controls="minimap" aria-pressed="false" hidden><svg viewBox="0 0 11 11" shape-rendering="crispEdges" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h11v1h-11zM0 10h11v1h-11zM0 1h1v9h-1zM10 1h1v9h-1zM3 3h5v1h-5zM3 6h5v1h-5zM3 4h1v2h-1zM7 4h1v2h-1z"/></svg></button>
    <button id="close" class="k-btn k-ico" type="button" aria-label="close" hidden><svg viewBox="0 0 11 11" shape-rendering="crispEdges" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M1 1h2v1h-2zM8 1h2v1h-2zM2 2h2v1h-2zM7 2h2v1h-2zM3 3h2v1h-2zM6 3h2v1h-2zM4 4h3v1h-3zM4 5h3v1h-3zM4 6h3v1h-3zM3 7h2v1h-2zM6 7h2v1h-2zM2 8h2v1h-2zM7 8h2v1h-2zM1 9h2v1h-2zM8 9h2v1h-2z"/></svg></button>
  </div>
  {# The explore hint and the visitor tally are no longer screen chrome:
     they live ON the canvas, etched below the hero doors (app.js builds
     #etched into #scene), so they pan and zoom with the world. #}
  {# role=dialog without aria-modal: the topbar (burger x, omni search) stays
     interactive while a sheet is open, and aria-modal would hide it from
     assistive tech. The canvas itself is excluded via scene.inert instead.
     A direct load of /work, /feed or /about SSRs the sheet already open;
     app.js adopts it instead of repainting, and no-JS readers get the full
     content and real links. #}
  {# The minimap (BIBLE.md section 8): the world as a plan in the corner,
     drawn by app.js in the two inks; a drag on it moves the camera. Chrome,
     so the watch density hides it with the bar. Ships hidden: styled like a
     tile, it would paint as an empty one until the module boots (#242). #}
  <canvas id="minimap" width="192" height="168" role="img" aria-label="map of the canvas; drag to move the view" hidden></canvas>
  </nav>
  <div id="modal" role="dialog"{% if sheet %} class="open{% if sheet.full %} fullpage{% endif %}{% if sheet.reading %} reading{% endif %}" aria-label="{{ sheet.title }}"{% endif %}><div id="backdrop"></div><div id="mscroll"><div id="gap"></div><div id="sheet" tabindex="-1">{% if sheet and sheet.bar %}{{ sheet.bar | safe }}{% endif %}<div class="inner" id="sheetInner">{% if sheet %}{% if sheet.pixel %}{{ sheet.title | pixelTitle }}{% else %}<h1>{{ sheet.title }}</h1>{% endif %}<div class="meta">{{ sheet.meta }}{% if sheet.tagRow %}{{ sheet.tagRow | safe }}{% endif %}</div>{{ sheet.body | safe }}{% endif %}</div></div></div></div>
  </div>

{# Live tile data, inert JSON under CSP script-src 'self'; app.js reads it.
   safeJson escapes "</" so the payload can never close its own tag. #}
<script type="application/json" id="boot">{{ boot | safeJson | safe }}</script>
<script type="module" src="{{ asset('/canvas/app.js') }}"></script>
{#- An SSR'd entry sheet runs its scripts as real tags: classic scripts keep
    declaration order during parse (an entry listing several gets them in the
    order it declared) and run after the sheet markup above exists, exactly the
    order mountEmbed reproduces client-side. #}
{%- if sheetAssets %}
{% for src in sheetAssets.js %}<script src="{{ src }}"></script>
{% endfor -%}
{% for src in sheetAssets.modules %}<script type="module" src="{{ src }}"></script>
{% endfor -%}
{% endif %}
</body>
</html>
